Welcome to the PLACE Advanced Development Software Version 2.70 from ICT Inc.. 
PLACE (PEEL Logic Architectural Compiler and Editor) is an enhanced 
development package that offers complete support for ICT's family of PEEL 
(Programmable Electrically Erasable Logic) Arrays and Devices.

*** New Versions of PLACE ***
The differences between Version 2.71 and Version 2.70 include:
(1) Added the new device option for PEEL22V10AZ.
(2) Added the PA7140 Jedec option for PLCC or DIP format.
(3) Remoted the obsolete device options from the menu.
(4) Consistent Pinout display between DESIGN and COMIPLE modules.
(5) Changed Optimization default level 5 to "Auto level 1-5" for PA7140.
(6) Revised the 85C220 and 85C224 translation algorithms.
(7) Revised the compilation algorithms for PEEL22CV8

*** System Requirements ***

- IBM PC,XT,AT, 386, 486 or compatible
- Minimum 540K RAM memory for most designs. Large designs may require
  up to 560K of free RAM.
- EGA, VGA, SVGA or Hercules Graphics
- At least 4.0 MB of hard disk free space
- Microsoft mouse or compatible with driver
- DOS version 3.0 or greater
- (Optional) Expanded Memory with LIM Specification Version 3.2 or greater.
- One additional communication port for PDS-2 and PDS-3 programmers.

*** Installation ***

-- Software Installation to Hard Disk --

1.  Turn the computer on.
2.  Boot-up DOS 3.0 or greater.
3.  Install your mouse driver first. PLACE will not boot-up without it.
4.  Insert the PLACE Install Disk into drive A. 
     Note: Do not write-protect this disk.
5.  At the prompt "A>", type "INSTAL" followed by the ENTER key. This
    copies all files from the diskette into the user-specified directory
    (directory defaults to "C:\ICTPLACE").
6.  After installation is completed, type "INIT" followed by the ENTER
    key.


Notes:
a.  For re-initialization, type "INIT" followed by the ENTER key.
b.  (Optional) Assuming the target hard disk drive is C, include the
    directory "C:\ICTPLACE" into your DOS Path and insert the statement
    "SET ICTPLACE=C:\ICTPLACE" into your AUTOEXEC.BAT file.
    This allows you to call up PLACE from any directory.
c.  If you are going to use the ICT PDS-3 programmer, please install the PDS-3
    software followed by the completion of the PLACE installation.


*** Notes for Non-Logitech and Non-Microsoft mouse users ***

In order to have the PLACE software running successfully on your computer, ICT 
strongly recommends using the Logitech or Microsoft mouse and driver to run 
the software. 


*** Notes for PEEL Array Applications Designer ***

In order to have PLACE DESIGN software running properly, please label the LCCs
and IOs prior to configuring the LCCs and IOs.

*** Notes for MS DOS 5.0 (or greater) users ***

- Minimize the usage of the TSR programs (e.g., PC pop-up calculator program), 
  so that the computer can have more free memory to run the software.
- Because DOS will not tell you if the procedure is successful or not, 
  be sure that your computer has enough upper memory available before 
  you load any TSR programs,e.g.,
            
            LOADHIGH(LH) PC-CALC.EXE (Load PC-CALC.EXE into upper memory)

  
  If not, the program will occupy the conventional memory instead. The easy 
  way to find out if the program is loaded into upper memory area or not is
  to enter the command
        MEM /C
  and note the program's location in memory.


*** Notes for Dr. DOS 6.0 users ***

If you have the Dr. DOS 6.0 operating system, please read the file DRDOS6.DOC
before installing the PLACE software.

*** Notes for PDS-3 programmer users ***

In order to interface with PLACE properly, please use PDS-3 Version 1.18 or 
greater. For upgrade information, please contact ICT technical support.

*** Notes for Logitech mouse driver Version 6.0 or higher ***

If you have a Logitech mouse with driver Version 6.0 or higher, please turn off
the " Video Overlay" switch by appending "NOVCI" to the mouse command in the
AUTOEXEC.BAT file. for example
     OLD                  NEW
 -----------         -----------------------------   
 ...                 ...
 mouse               mouse novci
 ...                 ...

and re-boot the computer.

*** PLACE Glossary ***

Listed below are common terms the PLACE manual uses:

Click    - press left button of mouse and release immediately.
           This mouse action is mostly used to select a feature or mode. It is
           sometimes used to emulate the ENTER key (for instance, after
           entering a label in the "Label" mode).
Click-R  - press right button of mouse and release immediately.
           Usually used to abort or quit a function or mode. A special function
           for this mouse action is to toggle between two modes, such as 
           between "Edit Arch" and "Edit Eqn" modes in the Design operation, 
           and between normal and "Edit" mode in the Simulate operation.
Click-LH - press left button and hold it down while moving the mouse cursor
           to a desired location. Release mouse button when destination is
           reached. Used in the scrolling from a LCC (or IOC) to another LCC,
           or in selecting a "Zoom" window in the Simulate operation.
LCC      - Logic Control Cell (PEEL Arrays only).
IOC      - I/O Cell.
INC      - Input Cell (PA7140 and PA7128 devices only)
GBC      - Global Cell (PEEL Arrays only).
RT       - (Register Type) Dynamic Register Control (PEEL Arrays only).
Reset    - Global Reset for the LCC flip-flop (PEEL Arrays only).
Preset   - Global Preset for the LCC flip-flop (PEEL Arrays only).
PCLKA,
PCLKB    - Global product term clocks for the IOC flip-flop (PEEL Arrays only).


